# Case: Real guest HTML, PNG and file clipboard roundtrip
# Mode: native
# Environment: disposable-guest
# Purpose: Prove native MIME capture and application without shared-clipboard propagation.
# Steps:
#   Offer synthetic HTML, PNG and a task-owned file through wl-copy; read production history; replace the offer; select its real history row and restore through physical Enter; read wl-paste.
# Expected:
#   Exact payload bytes survive capture and restore; each offer creates one history entry; restore produces no echo; the original file remains intact.
# Forbidden:
#   Directory clipboard substitution, host clipboard access, target insertion claims or directory-transfer acceptance claims.

system-board-write 'UNIC-D formats startup baseline'
start
system-format-roundtrip html
system-format-roundtrip png
system-format-roundtrip file
history-count 3
screenshot formats-restored-without-echo
